00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.400
I can't think of one at all!

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.820
Right?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.940
Seriously? You never thought of one?

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.120
Well, we were getting by
just as Yuigaoka's school idols.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.120
Keke-<i>chan </i>did use Kuukaa
in the beginning, but...

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.080
Precisely!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:01.880
So now that there are five of us,
we'll need Kuukaa's successor!

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.210
Let's take all of our initials!

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.460
"Chikerekasu"

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.260
Chikerekasu?

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.470
It sounds like internet slang.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.380
Cursed...

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.300
What?!

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.140
Well that's what it
sounds like! Look! "<i>Kasu</i>"!

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.470
Did you think of anything, Chi-<i>chan</i>?

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:20.060
I think we should go with... Maru.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.640
Maru?

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.650
For example...

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:25.230
Maru Maru Circle!

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.530
Circle means a ring, right?

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.030
So we can have circles come together

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:31.150
